{{As of|2023}}, '''[[Lagos]]''' is the largest city in the continent of [[Africa]] as well as in [[Nigeria]], a country where it was the capital.<ref>{{cite web | last=Douglas | first=Andrew | title=10 Largest Cities In Africa | website=WorldAtlas | date=2023-02-15 | url=https://www.worldatlas.com/cities/10-largest-cities-in-africa.html | access-date=2025-10-26}}</ref> In a 2022 report by ''Business Africa Insider'', the city is the fourth wealthiest city in Africa after [[Johannesburg]], [[CapeTown|Cape Town]] and [[Cairo]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Oluwole |first=Victor |date=2022-04-14 |title=Top 10 wealthiest cities in Africa |url=https://africa.businessinsider.com/local/lifestyle/top-10-wealthiest-cities-in-africa/2l5l5t4 |access-date=2022-10-11 |website=Business Insider Africa}}</ref>

